TI  - Improving construction contract question answering through embedding optimization and semantic chunking in large language models
AU  - Zhang, Lanqian
AU  - Ning, Yan
T2  - Advanced Engineering Informatics
AB  - Construction contract question answering (QA) is a knowledge-intensive task and requires timely responses to inquiries from multiple parties, but faces challenges in both accuracy and efficiency. Large Language Models (LLMs) excel at general-domain QA, but often show biases and hallucinations in specific domains. Although Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) improves LLMs’ performance with external knowledge, its effectiveness is limited due to the scarcity of domain-specific data and the poor segmentation and organization of documents. To address these challenges, this research proposes a domain-adapted RAG strategy for construction contracts (CC-RAG) to enhance QA performance. The core improvements of CC-RAG include two aspects. First, this research employs a hierarchical approach to transform normative construction contract documents into structured basic knowledge units. High-quality ‘‘question-knowledge’’ pairs are then automatically generated using online LLMs. These pairs are used to fine-tune the embedding model for domain adaptation, improving semantic retrieval accuracy. Second, knowledge units are automatically segmented based on semantic similarity. They are organized using hierarchical clustering to form coherent chunk structures, improving both integrity and accessibility of the retrieved knowledge. The evaluation results show that CCRAG achieves performance gains of 0.5% to 20% over base LLMs and traditional RAG strategies in construction contract QA tasks. Furthermore, CC-RAG can be deployed on a local 7B-parameter model while outperforming a 671B-parameter online model by 4 percentage points in QA accuracy. These findings demonstrate that CC-RAG improves QA performance. It also achieves a cost-effective balance of performance, offering a viable solution for deploying small-scale models in intelligent construction management.
